@@ -616,3 +616,20 @@ and out-of-scope item IDs return invalid params (`-32602`) with
 Omitted or null cursors preserve normal first-page behavior. Continue anchored
 pages with the returned opaque string `nextCursor`; response fields and
 `backwardsCursor` semantics are unchanged.
+
+
+### Bounded external supervision notices
+
+`thread/notice/append` records exact-thread external supervision context and a
+replayable agent display event without scheduling a user/model turn or changing
+native goals or usage. Text is bounded to 768 UTF-8 bytes and must end with
+`[External supervision event EVENT_ID]`; event IDs are 1–128 ASCII letters,
+digits, underscores or hyphens. Repeating an identical ID/text does not append
+or publish again; conflicting text is refused.
+
+`thread/notice/read` returns the exact retained notice and separately reports
+whether its context is still present in current model history. Append reports
+`notificationPublished` only after a subscribed connection confirms a write within
+the bounded publication interval. That field is not rendering or human-read
+proof. A missing write acknowledgement does not undo the retained notice or
+permit blind replay; reconnecting clients can replay the durable display event.
